WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.400
-Welcome back.
It is great to see you again.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.467
-Good to see you too, Jimmy.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.767
-We've known each other
for a long time.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.133
-Yeah, man. You've been
a supporter since day one.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.834
-I love you, bud.
-Yeah.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.200
-I want to talk about
this documentary.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.200
-Yeah.
-Yeah, "A Man Named Scott."

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.300
Can I call you Scott?
-Yeah, I would prefer that.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.868
-Okay. You would?
-Yeah, that's what I

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.734
introduce myself as to -- to my
friends when I meet people.

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.133
-You do?
-Yeah.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.767
-Where did "Kid Cudi" come from?

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:26.667
-Well, um, it's interesting.
My -- My first rap name

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:29.400
when I first started when I was
like 15 was "Lil Scott"

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.934
'cause I just didn't have,
like -- I don't know.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.133
I just was a big fan
of Lil Wayne at the time.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.534
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.000
Yep, there's Lil Wayne.
He's like --

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.033
-And we were, like,
close in age, so I was --

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.701
"Oh, this is a young dude
doing his thing, you know?

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.567
That's -- That's pretty cool."
So it started off as Lil Scott.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.934
But then, from there,
I wanted something a little bit

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.434
more personal, so I thought,
like, you know, using my --

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:51.434
my last name in some way
would be cool.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:54.534
So it ended up being, like,
"Kid Mesc,"

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.234
the first half of my last name,
right?

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.601
-Yeah.
-But, like, people kept

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.501
confusing it and thinking I was
saying, like, "Kid Mess."

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:01.901
-Like, "Kid Mess."
-So, like, that would really --

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.334
that would really, like,
make me upset.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.067
-You're like,
"No, I'm not saying I'm a mess."

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.300
Yeah.
-Yeah. Yeah, it's like, "No, no.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.934
It's -- It's Kid Mesc --
It's -- Never mind."

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.367
-Never mind.
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:11.634
You can't keep
explaining your name.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:14.434
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
So, like, as I was doing songs

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.601
and for -- for a mixtape
I was working on,

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.501
like, before the record,
you know how you get amped up

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:20.200
and you say your name, you know?
You say your rap name

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.334
just to announce, like,
this is your record, right?

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.667
-Of course.
-So it would always go like,

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.267
"Kid Mesc," you know?
And then it went from "Kid Mesc"

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.968
to "Kid Mescudi."
And then, like, it went from

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:31.200
"Kid Mescudi" to "Kid Cudi"!

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.734
And I was like,
"Oh, this works!" It's like --

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.167
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, like, "Stop there."

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.734
-I found it, yeah.
Yeah.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:37.734
-But is it "Mescudi"?
-All right, yeah.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:38.901
So I'm a -- so this is --
This is --

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:40.868
We gonna do this right now.
-Thank you.

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:43.167
-I really --
I really want everybody to --

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:45.000
to learn how to pronounce
my last name.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.200
This has been bothering me
for 13 years.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.634
-This is fantastic.
All right.

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:49.901
-So this is what it is.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.501
I know I kind of confuse
everybody with my rap name.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:54.467
But it's "Mes-cuh-dee."
"Mes-cuh-dee."

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.767
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:56.968
I mean,
I'm just calling you Scott.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:58.534
So, this is perfect.
Yeah, yeah. We're good.

00:01:58.534 --> 00:01:59.734
All right.
So it's good to know that now.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.133
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-But if you --

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.501
We got to watch the documentary.
I mean, this is --

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:06.801
It's -- It's phenomenal.
It's fantastic to see

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.801
where you came from
and where you ended up.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:11.367
It's just a --
It's a great American story.

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.868
You grew up in Ohio, right?
-Yeah, yeah. Cleveland.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:17.367
-Yeah, Cleveland, Ohio.
And then you came to New York.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.667
Is it here
where you worked at Applebee's?

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.667
-No, that was in Cleveland.
-That's in Cleveland.

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.033
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.767
-I love that someone
got their start at Applebee's.

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:25.801
-Yeah, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:28.667
Applebee's, like --
-I love that.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.601
